# CWC Canonical Asset Registry v1.0

# Introduction

The **Coz We Care Canonical Asset Registry (CWC-CAR)** is the authoritative registry of every Canonical Asset Object within the Coz We Care ecosystem.

As the identity foundation of the Canonical Asset System, CWC-CAR establishes a single, permanent, and authoritative registry for all Canonical Asset Objects. Every registered object receives a unique **Canonical Object Identifier (Object ID)** that serves as its immutable identity throughout its entire lifecycle.

The registry exists to ensure that every Canonical Asset Object is uniquely identifiable, consistently classified, and permanently traceable. By separating object identity from specification and visual representation, CWC-CAR provides a stable architectural foundation that enables the ecosystem to evolve without compromising canonical consistency.

Within the Coz We Care Canonical Asset System, CWC-CAR serves as the first authoritative step in the canonical lifecycle. Before an asset can be specified or represented, it must first be recognized as a Canonical Asset Object and formally registered within this registry. This principle guarantees that identity is established before documentation, implementation, or visual representation.

CWC-CAR operates in close coordination with the **CWC Canonical Asset Bible (CWC-CAB)** and the **CWC Canonical Reference Sheet (CWC-CRS)**. While these companion projects define the specification and visual reference of each asset, the ownership of Canonical Object Identifiers remains exclusively within CWC-CAR. Neither CWC-CAB nor CWC-CRS may create, modify, or reassign Canonical Object Identifiers.

This separation of responsibilities embodies the core architectural principles of the Coz We Care Canonical Asset System, including **Single Source of Truth**, **One Concept, One Home**, **Registry Before Specification**, **Registry Before Reference**, and **One Object, One Identifier**.

Ultimately, the purpose of CWC-CAR is not merely to catalog Canonical Asset Objects, but to establish a durable identity infrastructure that enables every Canonical Asset to remain uniquely identifiable, interoperable, and consistently governed across the entire Coz We Care knowledge architecture.

---

# Purpose

The purpose of the **Coz We Care Canonical Asset Registry (CWC-CAR)** is to establish and maintain the authoritative identity registry for every Canonical Asset Object within the Coz We Care ecosystem.

CWC-CAR serves as the single authoritative source for the registration, identification, and classification of Canonical Asset Objects. Every object recognized by the Canonical Asset System shall be registered within CWC-CAR before any canonical specification or reference representation is created.

The registry ensures that each Canonical Asset Object possesses one permanent and immutable **Canonical Object Identifier (Object ID)** throughout its entire lifecycle. This stable identity enables consistent referencing, traceability, interoperability, and governance across all canonical documentation.

CWC-CAR is responsible for maintaining the identity of Canonical Asset Objects independently of their specifications, implementations, or visual representations. By separating identity from documentation, the registry provides a stable architectural foundation that allows Canonical Assets to evolve without affecting their canonical identity.

As the identity authority of the Canonical Asset System, CWC-CAR supports the integrity of the broader knowledge architecture by eliminating duplicate identities, preserving object continuity, and ensuring that every Canonical Asset Object can be uniquely identified and consistently referenced across all related canonical projects.

Ultimately, the purpose of CWC-CAR is to provide a scalable, reliable, and enduring registry that safeguards the identity of every Canonical Asset Object while serving as the foundational layer upon which the CWC Canonical Asset Bible (CWC-CAB) and the CWC Canonical Reference Sheet (CWC-CRS) are built.

---

# Scope

The scope of the **Coz We Care Canonical Asset Registry (CWC-CAR)** is limited exclusively to the management of Canonical Asset Object identity within the Coz We Care Canonical Asset System.

CWC-CAR governs the registration, identification, classification, lifecycle, and relationships of Canonical Asset Objects. It defines the authoritative registry that establishes the existence and identity of every registered object, independent of how that object is specified, implemented, or visually represented.

The scope of CWC-CAR includes:

- Canonical Asset Object registration
- Canonical Object Identifier (Object ID) assignment
- Object classification
- Registry hierarchy
- Object relationships
- Registry lifecycle management
- Registry governance
- Registry integrity
- Registry traceability

CWC-CAR does not define the canonical specifications, implementation details, production guidance, technical standards, design rules, AI prompts, or visual representations of registered objects. These responsibilities belong to their respective canonical projects.

Specifically:

- **CWC Canonical Asset Bible (CWC-CAB)** defines the canonical specifications, architecture, standards, and governance associated with registered objects.
- **CWC Canonical Reference Sheet (CWC-CRS)** provides the canonical visual reference and representation of registered objects.

By maintaining a strict separation between identity, specification, and representation, CWC-CAR preserves the architectural integrity of the Canonical Asset System and ensures that every Canonical Asset Object possesses a single, stable, and authoritative identity throughout its lifecycle.

